More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (881–890)
881. Improper Validation of Password Strength Enforcement
Weak Password Policy
Applications allow weak passwords that can be easily guessed or brute-forced.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
882. Insecure Handling of User Role Assignment APIs
User Role Escalation
Attackers assign themselves higher privileges such as admin roles.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
883. Improper Validation of File Sharing Permissions
File Sharing Authorization Bypass
Attackers access files shared between other users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
884. Insecure Handling of Temporary Download Links
Temporary Link Exposure
Temporary download URLs remain valid longer than intended or can be guessed.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
885. Improper Validation of API Bulk Operations
Bulk API Authorization Bypass
Bulk endpoints perform actions on multiple accounts without proper permission checks.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
886. Insecure Handling of User Import Tools
User Import Vulnerability
Malicious CSV or data imports trigger system errors or inject unwanted records.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
887. Improper Validation of Application Settings APIs
Settings Manipulation Vulnerability
Attackers change application settings belonging to other users or organizations.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
888. Insecure Handling of Comment Moderation APIs
Comment Moderation Bypass
Attackers bypass comment filters or moderation systems.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
889. Improper Validation of User Profile Visibility
Private Profile Information Disclosure
Private user profile data becomes visible to unauthorized users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
890. Insecure Handling of Activity Feed APIs
